  "term": "neuronal transmission",
  "definition": "Neuronal transmission is the process by which one nerve cell passes a signal to another across a connection between them. The signal is conveyed either by releasing neurotransmitters or by direct electrical flow through specialized channels, and it is fundamental to how neurons work.",
